WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:03.551
KATARA: Water.

00:04.969 --> 00:06.012
Earth.

00:06.846 --> 00:07.889
Fire.

00:08.973 --> 00:10.016
Air.

00:11.184 --> 00:15.146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.396 --> 00:18.775
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.651 --> 00:22.487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.570 --> 00:23.780
could stop them.

00:23.863 --> 00:26.699
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

00:27.325 --> 00:29.786
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.869 --> 00:32.872
the new Avatar, an airbender named Aang.

00:32.956 --> 00:35.166
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.250 --> 00:37.502
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.627 --> 00:38.836
AANG: Oof!

00:38.920 --> 00:42.090
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:42.465 --> 00:44.467
♪

00:47.949 --> 00:49.951
♪

00:56.457 --> 00:59.377
( BOILING )

01:02.213 --> 01:03.881
Line 'em up for the warden!

01:03.965 --> 01:07.260
♪

01:12.682 --> 01:13.891
Dad.

01:15.268 --> 01:16.727
Excuse me, coming through!

01:16.811 --> 01:18.563
The warden wants me over there, sorry!

01:20.815 --> 01:23.401
WARDEN: Welcome to the Boiling Rock.

01:23.484 --> 01:25.736
I'm sure you've all heard
the horrible rumors

01:25.820 --> 01:27.780
about our little island.

01:27.864 --> 01:31.451
Well, I just want to tell you
that they don't have to be true,

01:31.534 --> 01:34.620
as long as you do everything I say.

01:35.288 --> 01:37.748
Look me in the eye
when I'm talking to you.

01:38.249 --> 01:39.459
No.

01:39.542 --> 01:42.879
Oh, you'd rather look at my shoes?

01:43.004 --> 01:44.422
Then take a look!

01:44.881 --> 01:46.174
Aah!

01:47.508 --> 01:51.429
I know exactly who you are,
Hakoda of the Water Tribe.

01:51.512 --> 01:53.431
So strong-willed.

01:53.514 --> 01:57.059
But don't worry.
We'll get rid of that in time.

01:57.143 --> 01:58.978
Now look me in the eye!

01:59.061 --> 02:00.980
( WATER BOILING )

02:03.024 --> 02:05.151
See, isn't that better?

02:05.234 --> 02:08.321
You will all do as I say or pay the price.

02:08.404 --> 02:10.198
You will always... ( GRUNTS )

02:10.281 --> 02:11.491
( SPUTTERS )

02:12.825 --> 02:15.536
- Are you okay, sir?
- I'm fine!

02:15.620 --> 02:18.080
Get these prisoners out of my sight.

02:18.164 --> 02:20.917
♪

02:29.884 --> 02:30.968
( DOOR OPENS )

02:33.387 --> 02:35.223
Thank goodness you're okay!

02:35.348 --> 02:40.436
If you take one step closer,
you'll see just how okay I am.

02:40.520 --> 02:41.938
Dad, it's me.

02:43.272 --> 02:44.482
Sokka?

02:45.149 --> 02:46.567
My son.

02:47.735 --> 02:49.654
( CHUCKLES ) You know, Sokka,

02:49.779 --> 02:52.281
you should be more careful
with that guard outfit on.

02:52.365 --> 02:53.991
I almost punched you in the gut.

02:54.075 --> 02:56.619
Yeah, I ran into that problem earlier.

02:56.702 --> 02:59.622
( FOOTSTEPS )

03:00.331 --> 03:01.541
( CLANK )

03:03.000 --> 03:05.211
Are you comfortable, Chit Sang?

03:05.294 --> 03:07.880
If you're trying to get me
to talk, forget it!

03:07.964 --> 03:09.340
I'm not a squealer.

03:10.675 --> 03:13.553
Chit Sang, I only ask you
if you were comfortable.

03:13.636 --> 03:16.847
Well, yeah, actually,
I am pretty comfortable.

03:17.723 --> 03:18.891
( GRUNTS )

03:20.476 --> 03:22.061
WARDEN: Are you still comfortable?

03:22.144 --> 03:23.187
No.

03:23.271 --> 03:25.690
WARDEN: I know you and your cronies
are not smart enough

03:25.773 --> 03:28.276
to come up with that little escape plan.

03:28.359 --> 03:31.445
So you're gonna tell me who is.

03:31.529 --> 03:33.531
( TENSE MUSIC )

03:36.033 --> 03:38.035
♪

03:44.584 --> 03:46.210
SOKKA: So where's Bato?

03:46.294 --> 03:48.129
Where's everyone else from the invasion?

03:48.212 --> 03:49.547
The others are being held

03:49.630 --> 03:51.507
at a prison near the Fire Nation palace.

03:51.591 --> 03:54.135
They singled me out as their leader
and sent me here.

03:54.385 --> 03:55.845
But before I left,

03:55.928 --> 03:58.389
I met some young women
who said they knew you.

03:58.472 --> 04:00.558
The Oshinama Fighters?

04:00.641 --> 04:03.561
- You mean the Kyoshi Warriors?
- That's right.

04:03.644 --> 04:06.772
Their leader, Suki, is here,
and she's gonna escape with us.

04:06.856 --> 04:09.066
Good, we'll need all the help we can get.

04:09.150 --> 04:12.320
- And you know Prince Zuko?
- The son of the Fire Lord?

04:12.403 --> 04:14.739
I don't know him, but I know of him.

04:14.822 --> 04:18.284
- Well, he's here, too.
- Sounds like a major problem.

04:18.367 --> 04:20.494
Actually, he's on our side now.

04:22.371 --> 04:24.373
I know, I had the same reaction.

04:24.457 --> 04:26.667
After all he's done,
it was hard to trust him.

04:26.751 --> 04:28.252
But he's really proven himself,

04:28.336 --> 04:30.588
and I never would've found you
without his help.

04:31.672 --> 04:34.133
So, do you have a plan?

04:34.216 --> 04:35.509
We had one,

04:35.593 --> 04:38.179
but some of the other prisoners
got involved and ruined it.

04:38.262 --> 04:40.806
I don't know if there's
another way off this island.

04:40.890 --> 04:43.351
Sokka, there's no prison in the world

04:43.434 --> 04:45.603
that can hold two Water Tribe geniuses.

04:45.728 --> 04:47.855
Then we better find two.

04:48.564 --> 04:50.566
( LAUGHS )

04:50.650 --> 04:52.610
( CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY )

04:53.778 --> 04:55.780
( TENSE MUSIC )

04:58.032 --> 05:00.034
♪

05:02.036 --> 05:03.871
Zuko, are you there?

05:03.954 --> 05:05.373
I'm here.

05:05.456 --> 05:07.333
I just got done talking to my dad.

05:07.416 --> 05:09.293
We came up with an escape plan together.

05:09.377 --> 05:11.128
MALE GUARD: What are you doing here?

05:12.713 --> 05:15.800
I was just telling this dirty
lowlife what I think of him!

05:15.883 --> 05:17.677
Well, you'll have to do that later.

05:17.760 --> 05:18.969
He's coming with us.

05:19.053 --> 05:20.596
Why?

05:20.680 --> 05:22.640
Because we have orders
straight from the warden,

05:22.723 --> 05:23.891
that's why.

05:23.974 --> 05:26.811
Could I just get 10 more seconds
to rough him up a bit?

05:27.770 --> 05:29.397
Fine, 10 seconds.

05:30.064 --> 05:31.982
( OPENS AND SHUTS DOOR )

05:32.066 --> 05:34.402
SOKKA: Take that! And this!

05:34.485 --> 05:35.528
Newbie!

05:35.820 --> 05:38.280
( ZUKO GRUNTING )

05:40.032 --> 05:42.576
We have a new plan, but it's
gonna need a big distraction.

05:42.660 --> 05:44.787
- Be in the yard in one hour.
-( DOOR OPENS )

05:46.288 --> 05:47.415
( GROANING )

05:47.498 --> 05:49.667
All right, that's enough.

05:52.086 --> 05:55.005
ZUKO: What are you doing?
Where are you taking me?

05:56.590 --> 06:00.469
Aah! I didn't do anything wrong.

06:00.594 --> 06:03.764
Come on, Zuko. We all know that's a lie.

06:03.848 --> 06:04.974
Mai.

06:07.059 --> 06:09.061
( FOOTSTEPS )

06:11.814 --> 06:15.276
- How is he?
- I think he's ready to talk.

06:15.359 --> 06:17.153
( GROANS )

06:17.236 --> 06:20.531
( PANTS )

06:20.614 --> 06:24.285
Have you had enough time
to think about what I asked?

06:24.535 --> 06:26.454
- Yes.
- And?

06:26.537 --> 06:28.205
You're right.

06:28.289 --> 06:31.041
There was another person
involved in the escape plan.

06:31.125 --> 06:32.168
Who?

06:32.251 --> 06:34.545
It's a guy who's disguised
like a prison guard,

06:34.628 --> 06:36.422
only he's not a prison guard.

06:36.505 --> 06:39.717
He's the mastermind.
He came up with the plan.

06:53.898 --> 06:57.693
- How did you know I was here?
- Because I know you so well.

06:57.777 --> 06:59.069
But how...

06:59.153 --> 07:01.155
The warden's my uncle, you idiot.

07:01.530 --> 07:02.823
( GROANS )

07:02.907 --> 07:06.160
The truth is, I guess I don't know you.

07:06.243 --> 07:07.703
All I get is a letter?

07:07.828 --> 07:09.538
You could've at least looked me in the eye

07:09.622 --> 07:11.165
when you ripped out my heart.

07:11.749 --> 07:14.251
- I didn't mean to...
- You didn't mean to?

07:15.085 --> 07:18.714
"Dear Mai, I'm sorry that
you have to find out this way,

07:18.798 --> 07:20.132
"but I'm leaving."

07:20.216 --> 07:22.259
Stop! This isn't about you!

07:22.343 --> 07:24.220
This is about the Fire Nation.

07:24.303 --> 07:27.723
Thanks, Zuko.
That makes me feel all better.

07:29.225 --> 07:31.769
Mai, I never wanted to hurt you.

07:32.186 --> 07:34.730
But I have to do this to save my country.

07:34.814 --> 07:37.650
Save it? You're betraying your country.

07:37.733 --> 07:39.360
That's not how I see it.

07:41.779 --> 07:43.781
( WHOOSHING )

07:49.036 --> 07:52.289
- Sokka, what's going on?
- I don't have much time.

07:52.373 --> 07:55.084
If I'm seen with you, the guards
might think something's up.

07:56.585 --> 07:59.421
- I just talked to my dad.
- That's great.

07:59.505 --> 08:02.800
Yeah, and we're escaping
today... on the gondola.

08:02.883 --> 08:03.926
What?

08:04.009 --> 08:06.136
My dad and I came up
with the plan together.

08:06.220 --> 08:07.596
We're gonna commandeer the gondola

08:07.680 --> 08:09.181
and we're gonna take a hostage with us

08:09.265 --> 08:10.641
so they won't cut the lines.

08:10.724 --> 08:12.852
We'll never make it on to the gondola.

08:12.935 --> 08:14.603
There's too many guards.

08:14.687 --> 08:16.272
My dad already thought of that.

08:16.355 --> 08:18.065
He said we'll need a distraction.

08:18.148 --> 08:20.317
That's why we're gonna
start a prison riot.

08:21.527 --> 08:24.405
Okay, let's say by some
miracle this all works

08:24.488 --> 08:25.865
and we make it on the gondola.

08:25.948 --> 08:27.825
The warden will still just cut the lines

08:27.908 --> 08:29.493
even if we have a captive.

08:29.577 --> 08:32.162
Not if the warden is the captive.

08:32.454 --> 08:34.582
-( CLANKING )
-( FOOTSTEPS )

08:34.665 --> 08:36.375
I have to go.

08:36.458 --> 08:38.627
I'll find you before we start the riot.

08:41.589 --> 08:43.841
Hey, you! The warden wants to see you!

08:43.924 --> 08:44.967
Why?

08:45.050 --> 08:46.844
I don't know. I didn't ask.

08:46.927 --> 08:49.013
Maybe I could schedule
another time with him?

08:49.096 --> 08:50.222
How's tomorrow?

08:50.306 --> 08:52.516
He wants to see you now.

08:56.270 --> 08:57.855
WARDEN: Put him in the lineup.

09:00.608 --> 09:02.735
( WHIMPERS )

09:03.736 --> 09:05.321
WARDEN: One of you is an imposter

09:05.404 --> 09:08.157
who thought he could fool me.

09:08.240 --> 09:13.120
But now that person is going
to be in a lot of trouble.

09:14.580 --> 09:15.915
Who is it?

09:17.041 --> 09:19.043
( TEETH CHATTERING )

09:22.254 --> 09:24.882
CHIT SANG: That's him, Warden.
He's the imposter!

09:25.966 --> 09:27.051
What?

09:29.261 --> 09:30.679
I am not!

09:30.763 --> 09:33.307
He's lying! He's a liar!

09:33.390 --> 09:34.683
( FOOTSTEPS )

09:36.894 --> 09:38.062
( EXHALES )

09:40.856 --> 09:45.653
- I'm telling you, it wasn't me.
- Save your breath.

09:45.736 --> 09:47.488
I know you've been working together.

09:47.571 --> 09:50.616
You threw Chit Sang in the very
cooler they used to escape.

09:50.699 --> 09:52.785
It was all part of your plan.

09:52.868 --> 09:54.912
That was just a coincidence!

09:54.995 --> 09:56.038
( DOOR OPENS )

09:56.121 --> 09:57.581
Sir, there's someone to see you.

09:57.706 --> 09:59.625
Who told you to interrupt me?

10:01.001 --> 10:02.544
I did.

10:03.712 --> 10:05.255
WARDEN: Princess Azula!

10:05.339 --> 10:07.758
Uh, it is an honor to welcome you

10:07.841 --> 10:10.344
to the Fire Nation's
most exemplary prison.

10:10.427 --> 10:12.388
I didn't realize you were coming.

10:12.554 --> 10:14.014
Who is this?

10:14.723 --> 10:15.933
He's a guard

10:16.016 --> 10:18.519
who was involved in a recent
and feeble escape attempt.

10:18.602 --> 10:21.605
- It wasn't me!
- Quiet, you!

10:21.689 --> 10:24.024
You're wasting your time.
That's not one of them.

10:25.234 --> 10:27.903
- How do you know?
- Because I'm a people person.

10:29.238 --> 10:30.614
( CLANK )

10:30.698 --> 10:32.449
( FOOTSTEPS )

10:34.159 --> 10:35.577
Hey, I just got orders.

10:35.661 --> 10:37.329
Let the prisoners out into the yard.

10:37.413 --> 10:39.164
But we're in the middle of lockdown.

10:39.289 --> 10:40.457
Oh, okay.

10:40.582 --> 10:42.334
I'll just go tell the
warden you said that.

10:42.626 --> 10:43.877
I'm sure he'll be glad

10:43.961 --> 10:45.838
to hear about you
undermining his authority.

10:45.921 --> 10:47.381
What's your name again?

10:47.506 --> 10:49.675
Wait, uh, don't tell the warden.

10:49.758 --> 10:51.176
I'm just a little confused.

10:51.301 --> 10:53.137
Hey, I'm confused, too.

10:53.220 --> 10:55.931
But the warden's in a
bad mood and irrational.

10:56.056 --> 10:57.558
So if you ask me,

10:57.683 --> 11:00.686
it's best not to question it
and just do what he says.

11:01.145 --> 11:02.938
Yeah, you're right.

11:03.313 --> 11:05.524
- We're letting them out!
-( BELL RINGING )

11:18.787 --> 11:20.831
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

11:22.916 --> 11:25.377
This is it. We have to start a riot.

11:25.461 --> 11:27.337
Okay, but how do we do that?

11:27.421 --> 11:29.214
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

11:32.259 --> 11:33.260
I'll show you.

11:35.763 --> 11:36.764
( GRUNTS )

11:36.847 --> 11:39.016
Hey! What did you do that for?

11:39.099 --> 11:40.476
That hurt my feelings.

11:40.559 --> 11:41.977
Aren't you mad at me?

11:42.061 --> 11:44.188
Uh, well, normally I would be,

11:44.271 --> 11:46.774
but I've been learning
to control my anger.

11:46.857 --> 11:47.900
( SQUEAKING )

11:47.983 --> 11:49.234
This isn't working.

11:49.318 --> 11:50.527
Hey, you!

11:50.611 --> 11:52.613
You're lucky I didn't rat you out.

11:52.696 --> 11:54.823
But my generosity comes with a price.

11:55.115 --> 11:58.702
I know you're planning another
escape attempt, and I want in.

11:59.078 --> 12:01.497
Actually, we're trying
to escape right now,

12:01.580 --> 12:02.998
but we need a riot.

12:03.082 --> 12:05.959
You wouldn't happen to know
how to start one, would you?

12:06.043 --> 12:08.337
A prison riot? Please.

12:08.962 --> 12:10.380
( GASPS )

12:12.549 --> 12:15.344
Hey! Riot!

12:15.552 --> 12:17.554
( PRISONERS SHOUTING )

12:20.432 --> 12:21.767
Impressive.

12:23.143 --> 12:24.770
Forget about controlling my anger.

12:24.853 --> 12:26.355
Let's riot! Whoa!

12:27.606 --> 12:28.649
( GRUNTS )

12:29.608 --> 12:31.235
( SHOOTING )

12:31.318 --> 12:33.070
( GRUNTING )

12:33.737 --> 12:35.697
WARDEN: Who let these
prisoners into the yard?

12:35.781 --> 12:38.033
This is supposed to be a lockdown!

12:39.368 --> 12:40.452
( SQUEAK )

12:40.536 --> 12:41.912
( TWINKLING )

12:43.288 --> 12:44.540
Ma'am, there's a riot going on.

12:44.623 --> 12:45.707
I'm here to protect you.

12:45.791 --> 12:49.670
- I don't need any protection.
- Heh, believe me, she doesn't.

12:49.753 --> 12:51.964
I'm sorry, but I'm under
direct orders from your uncle

12:52.047 --> 12:53.382
to make sure nothing happens.

12:53.465 --> 12:54.925
( FIRE RUMBLING )

12:55.217 --> 12:56.552
Get off of me!

13:04.268 --> 13:05.894
( SHOUTING )

13:05.978 --> 13:07.563
( SHOOTING )

13:11.441 --> 13:13.277
Zuko, good. We're all here.

13:13.360 --> 13:14.611
Now, all we need to do

13:14.695 --> 13:16.822
is grab the warden
and get to the gondolas.

13:16.905 --> 13:17.990
And how do we do that?

13:18.991 --> 13:20.450
I'm not sure.

13:20.534 --> 13:23.036
Ugh, I thought you'd thought this through!

13:23.120 --> 13:24.204
I thought you told me

13:24.288 --> 13:26.039
it's okay not to think everything through!

13:26.123 --> 13:29.334
Maybe not everything,
but this is kind of important.

13:30.294 --> 13:31.670
CHIT SANG: Hey, uh, fellas?

13:31.753 --> 13:33.589
I think your girlfriend's
taking care of it.

13:33.672 --> 13:35.632
( PRISONERS SHOUTING )

13:35.716 --> 13:37.134
( SHOOTING )

13:37.217 --> 13:39.219
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

13:40.429 --> 13:42.389
♪

13:48.061 --> 13:49.104
( GRUNTS )

13:49.188 --> 13:50.731
♪

14:03.660 --> 14:04.995
You wouldn't dare.

14:06.413 --> 14:07.581
( GRUNTS )

14:08.457 --> 14:11.376
Sorry, Warden. You're my prisoner now.

14:11.752 --> 14:13.045
( GRUNTS )

14:13.128 --> 14:15.339
We've got the warden.
Now let's get out of here.

14:15.422 --> 14:16.465
( PANTING )

14:16.548 --> 14:19.218
- That's some girl.
- Tell me about it.

14:29.019 --> 14:30.312
We're almost there.

14:33.607 --> 14:34.691
( GRUNTS )

14:34.775 --> 14:36.443
( FIRE RUMBLING )

14:37.486 --> 14:39.571
Back off! We've got the warden.

14:41.406 --> 14:42.449
( GRUNTS )

14:44.910 --> 14:46.119
Let's go.

14:46.203 --> 14:48.205
( TENSE MUSIC )

14:48.664 --> 14:51.667
♪

14:56.838 --> 14:57.923
Everyone in.

14:58.006 --> 15:00.008
♪

15:03.428 --> 15:04.888
( CLICKING )

15:04.972 --> 15:06.974
( CREAKING )

15:08.475 --> 15:10.435
( WHIRRING )

15:12.562 --> 15:14.731
( GRUNTS )

15:21.405 --> 15:22.948
( SHOOTING )

15:24.866 --> 15:26.952
( GROANS )

15:29.329 --> 15:30.622
What are you doing?

15:30.706 --> 15:32.874
I'm making it so they can't stop us.

15:32.958 --> 15:34.251
Way to think ahead.

15:34.334 --> 15:37.379
- SUKI: We're on our way.
- Wait, who's that?

15:38.797 --> 15:40.173
ZUKO: That's a problem.

15:40.257 --> 15:41.967
It's my sister and her friend.

15:42.050 --> 15:43.969
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

15:45.387 --> 15:47.389
♪

15:54.980 --> 15:56.815
( WHOOSH )

15:56.898 --> 15:58.900
♪

16:05.157 --> 16:07.784
This is a rematch I've been waiting for.

16:07.868 --> 16:08.869
Me too.

16:08.952 --> 16:10.704
♪

16:32.809 --> 16:35.270
( WHOOSHING )

16:39.399 --> 16:41.401
( GRUNTING )

16:47.699 --> 16:49.117
( GRUNTS )

16:50.035 --> 16:52.079
♪

16:57.042 --> 16:59.211
( WHOOSHING )

16:59.294 --> 17:01.463
♪

17:15.560 --> 17:17.062
( WARDEN GRUNTS )

17:17.145 --> 17:18.397
MALE GUARD: There's the warden.

17:18.480 --> 17:19.481
I see him!

17:20.399 --> 17:21.608
( WARDEN GRUNTS )

17:22.984 --> 17:24.778
Cut the line!

17:24.861 --> 17:26.321
He wants us to cut the line.

17:26.405 --> 17:29.366
But if we cut the line,
there's no way he'll survive.

17:29.449 --> 17:30.826
He knows that.

17:30.909 --> 17:32.911
( CREAKING )

17:34.413 --> 17:36.039
( BLASTS )

17:36.123 --> 17:38.125
♪

17:42.295 --> 17:44.297
( CREAKING )

17:47.175 --> 17:49.010
( GROANS )

17:50.303 --> 17:51.805
( PANTS )

17:56.726 --> 17:58.603
They're about to cut the line!

17:58.687 --> 18:00.105
♪

18:06.445 --> 18:08.447
( WHIRRING )

18:09.823 --> 18:11.700
Then it's time to leave.

18:13.535 --> 18:14.703
( BLAST )

18:14.786 --> 18:16.204
Goodbye, Zuko.

18:16.288 --> 18:17.664
( EERIE MUSIC )

18:17.747 --> 18:19.499
♪

18:29.926 --> 18:32.554
They're cutting the line!
The gondola's about to go!

18:32.637 --> 18:34.389
CHIT SANG: I hope this thing floats.

18:34.473 --> 18:36.099
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

18:36.183 --> 18:38.185
♪

18:43.648 --> 18:45.775
( GRUNTING )

18:45.859 --> 18:47.319
What are you doing?

18:48.111 --> 18:49.905
Saving the jerk who dumped me.

18:52.407 --> 18:54.117
( FIRE RUMBLING )

18:59.831 --> 19:00.957
( GROANING )

19:03.376 --> 19:04.503
Whoa!

19:04.586 --> 19:05.879
( GRUNTING )

19:07.839 --> 19:08.882
( GRUNTING )

19:11.051 --> 19:12.511
( CREAKING )

19:16.181 --> 19:17.474
Who is that?

19:22.938 --> 19:24.105
It's Mai.

19:24.189 --> 19:26.650
What is she doing?

19:26.733 --> 19:28.193
( "I DON'T KNOW" SOUND )

19:30.695 --> 19:32.697
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

19:32.781 --> 19:34.783
♪

19:39.579 --> 19:41.581
( GRUNTS )

19:43.667 --> 19:45.043
Sorry, Warden.

19:45.126 --> 19:47.546
Your record is officially broken.

19:48.129 --> 19:50.423
( GRUNTS )

19:51.007 --> 19:52.050
( PANTING )

19:52.133 --> 19:54.302
Well, we made it out. Now what?

19:56.596 --> 19:59.891
- Zuko, what are you doing?
- My sister was on that island.

19:59.975 --> 20:03.478
Yeah, and she's probably right
behind us, so let's not stop.

20:03.562 --> 20:05.564
What I mean is she must've
come here somehow.

20:07.857 --> 20:10.151
There! That's our way out of here.

20:10.235 --> 20:12.237
♪

20:19.369 --> 20:20.787
AZUKA: Leave us alone.

20:25.584 --> 20:27.627
I never expected this from you.

20:31.631 --> 20:33.967
The thing I don't understand is why.

20:34.050 --> 20:37.637
Why would you do it?
You know the consequences.

20:39.806 --> 20:41.391
I guess you just don't know people

20:41.474 --> 20:43.226
as well as you think you do.

20:43.310 --> 20:45.020
You miscalculated.

20:45.103 --> 20:47.689
I love Zuko more than I fear you.

20:48.356 --> 20:51.484
No, you miscalculated!
You should've feared me more!

20:55.447 --> 20:56.948
( GRUNTS )

20:59.451 --> 21:01.202
( GASPS )

21:03.163 --> 21:05.582
Come on! Let's get outta here!

21:09.669 --> 21:11.338
You're both fools!

21:13.632 --> 21:15.842
What shall we do with them, Princess?

21:15.925 --> 21:17.093
AZUKA: Put them somewhere

21:17.177 --> 21:20.889
I'll never have to see their
faces again, and let them rot!

21:21.556 --> 21:23.558
( CRICKETS CHIRPING )

21:29.147 --> 21:30.857
KATARA: What are you doing in this thing?

21:30.940 --> 21:32.442
What happened to the war balloon?

21:32.525 --> 21:33.777
It kinda got destroyed.

21:33.860 --> 21:36.237
Sounds like a crazy fishing trip.

21:36.321 --> 21:38.198
Did you at least get some good meat?

21:38.281 --> 21:41.159
I did, the best meat of all.

21:41.242 --> 21:44.037
The meat of friendship and fatherhood.

21:47.832 --> 21:50.126
I'm new. What's up, everybody?

21:50.210 --> 21:51.419
Dad.

21:52.462 --> 21:53.838
Hi, Katara.

21:58.551 --> 22:00.220
How are you here?

22:00.303 --> 22:02.764
What is going on? Where did you go?

22:02.847 --> 22:05.809
We kind of went to a Fire Nation prison.

22:05.892 --> 22:07.602
♪

22:10.814 --> 22:13.775
TOPH: Seriously,
you guys didn't find any meat?

22:13.858 --> 22:16.861
♪

22:28.498 --> 22:31.501
( MALE VOCALIZING DRUMBEATS )

22:40.135 --> 22:42.137
♪

22:54.899 --> 22:56.901
♪
